cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TomoSTAR, please cite it as below."
title: "TomoSTAR: seismic travel-time and attenuation tomography from the command line"
abstract: >-
  A standalone command-line program for local earthquake tomography: automatic picking,
  hypocentre relocation, minimum 1-D models, Vp, Vs and Vp/Vs travel-time tomography on regular or
  adaptive octree grids with fast-marching rays, Q tomography from t*, L-curves, resolution tests and
  the exact resolution matrix, standard deviations and resolution lengths on adaptive cells, with SIMD,
  OpenCL and MPI, scriptable pipelines and file exchange with QUIVER.
authors:
  - family-names: Mangiagalli
    given-names: Matteo
    affiliation: "Università degli Studi di Urbino Carlo Bo"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-2031-8729"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23188347
repository-code: "https://github.com/mattemangia/TomoSTAR"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-09
keywords:
  - seismic tomography
  - local earthquake tomography
  - attenuation tomography
  - t*
  - adaptive parameterisation
  - octree
  - resolution matrix
  - fast marching method
  - LSQR
  - OpenCL
  - earthquake location
